{
 "id": "rewrite+spend/extract-llm-sweep/ask-then-cold-apply/5m",
 "description": "A spent 8,000-token tool output (message 1) sits in a 17,500-token thread. At minute 6:20 the keep-alive ping is replaced by the sweep's ask: the previous turn's forwarded body plus a 400-token question, so it reads 17,500 tokens from the warm cache and renews the entry (400 input, 17,500 read, 200 output: -$0.00945). The model says drop; the verdict is held and changes no request while the cache is warm, because a removal inside the cached prefix would be a break. The keep-alive ends and the entry expires. The next request arrives 23 minutes later, past the 5m TTL of both the last request and the ask, so no rescue is credited and nothing is cached: the held verdict is applied and the 7,900 removed tokens (8,000 to a 100-token descriptor with a <<cg:HASH>> marker) are priced as cache writes, 7,900 x $3.75 = +$0.02963. The ask and the removal share one ChangeID. Total +$0.02018.",
